On macOS/Linux (`installAfterDownload` returns true): after download, it installs immediately, emits "installed", and the app is ready for restart.

On Windows (`installAfterDownload` returns false): after download, emits "download-finished-pending" (phase="ready", pendingInstall=true). The install happens only when the user clicks "Update & restart".

In the `retry()` path:
- If `downloaded && handle && snapshot.error` on Windows: `downloaded=true`, `handle` exists, `error` exists. It calls `handle.install()`. But on Windows, install needs the app to exit. Calling `install()` on Windows would launch the NSIS installer which exits the app. That might be OK actually.

